-- title:
--   Sections 5.2–5.5 — Eliminate minimal counterexamples
-- statement:
--   There is no minimal counterexample in the finite
--   planar, bridgeless, plain, precubic comparison class:
--   $$\forall n\ \forall H\text{ on }n\text{ darts},\quad
--   \neg\operatorname{MinimalCounterexample}(H).$$
--   There is no hypothesis granting a successful external program run, correctness
--   of a checker, reducibility of a catalogue, or validity of discharge rules.
--
--   Formalization note: the combined source-backed reducibility/unavoidability
--   endpoint. The source's conditional `unavoidability` is used only after proving
--   the genuine reducibility theorem. This remains the substantial finite-case-analysis
--   frontier: formalize configuration/contraction/Kempe semantics, the stronger
--   Birkhoff ring and embedding facts, a concrete source catalogue (633 entries in
--   the reference), sound finite checkers, all required certificate checks, and
--   the discharging case coverage. Structure and conservation alone do not prove it.
--
--   Notation: $D=\{0,\ldots,n-1\}$ is the dart set, $n = |D|$ its
--   size, and $p = \nu_H$ is the node permutation. Write $e,f$ for the edge and face
--   permutations, with $p(f(e(d)))=d$. Edge, node and face counts $E,N,F$ are numbers
--   of permutation orbits, including singleton orbits. The component count $C$ uses
--   the equivalence generated by all three permutations. Planarity means the exact
--   Euler equality $E+N+F=n+2C$, and connectedness means $C=1$.
--
--   A plain hypermap has a fixed-point-free involution $e$. Cubic means every node
--   orbit has size three; precubic means every node orbit has size at most three.
--   Bridgeless means $d$ and $e(d)$ never lie in the same face orbit. A $k$-coloring
--   is a map $D\to\{0,\ldots,k-1\}$ constant on face orbits and different across
--   each edge step. No requirement uses all available colors. The empty dart set
--   has zero components, is planar, and is colorable, but is not connected.
--
--   An admissible hypermap is planar, bridgeless, plain and precubic. A minimal
--   counterexample is a non-four-colorable admissible hypermap such that every
--   admissible hypermap with fewer darts is four-colorable. Minimality includes
--   all finite carriers through their enumeration by $\operatorname{Fin}(m)$;
--   cubicity, connectedness and lower face-degree bounds are not assumed.
--
--   Source: Georges Gonthier, A Computer-Checked Proof of the Four Colour Theorem (2005), https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/research/wp-content/uploads/2012/10/4colproof.pdf; Section 3, PDF p. 8, paragraph on PDF p. 8 listing reducibility and unavoidability; Section 5.2, PDF pp. 26–32; Section 5.4, PDF pp. 38–44; Section 5.5, PDF pp. 44–48. Relevant displays are unnumbered. Pinned executable reference: https://github.com/rocq-community/fourcolor/blob/c1d6b1cd5288bea4b067aac13cdde3c18dffe018/theories/proof/reducibility.v#L16; https://github.com/rocq-community/fourcolor/blob/c1d6b1cd5288bea4b067aac13cdde3c18dffe018/theories/proof/unavoidability.v#L20; https://github.com/rocq-community/fourcolor/blob/c1d6b1cd5288bea4b067aac13cdde3c18dffe018/theories/proof/configurations.v#L17.
-- source:
--   Georges Gonthier, A Computer-Checked Proof of the Four Colour Theorem (2005), https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/research/wp-content/uploads/2012/10/4colproof.pdf; Section 3, PDF p. 8, paragraph on PDF p. 8 listing reducibility and unavoidability; Section 5.2, PDF pp. 26–32; Section 5.4, PDF pp. 38–44; Section 5.5, PDF pp. 44–48. Relevant displays are unnumbered. Pinned executable reference: https://github.com/rocq-community/fourcolor/blob/c1d6b1cd5288bea4b067aac13cdde3c18dffe018/theories/proof/reducibility.v#L16; https://github.com/rocq-community/fourcolor/blob/c1d6b1cd5288bea4b067aac13cdde3c18dffe018/theories/proof/unavoidability.v#L20; https://github.com/rocq-community/fourcolor/blob/c1d6b1cd5288bea4b067aac13cdde3c18dffe018/theories/proof/configurations.v#L17.

import Definitions.Def_FourColor_Hypermap

namespace FourColor
universe u
theorem no_minimal_counterexample :
  ∀ (n : ℕ) (H : Hypermap n), ¬ H.MinimalCounterexample := by sorry
end FourColor
